[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/tests/task_queue_impl_test.py: The verification harness cannot import this suite: the suite's module-level resolution of the implementation is shadowed by the top-level task_queue module namespace exposed by the low-level specification, so the suite aborts before any test executes and none of the contracted behavior in low/task_queue.pyi or low/task_queue_impl.pyi is exercised. Ensure the suite resolves the implementation modules without relying on a package-qualified path that is shadowed by the top-level module namespace, so the contracted invariants (capacity 10, empty/full/available, pending_count) and positive-path postconditions (submit appends and grows pending_count, dispatch pops the oldest and invokes the worker, complete/get_outcome recording, clear purging) are actually verified.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/task_queue/tests/task_worker_impl_test.py: The verification harness cannot import this suite: the suite's module-level resolution of the implementation is shadowed by the top-level task_queue and task_worker module namespaces exposed by the low-level specification, so the suite aborts before any test executes and none of the contracted behavior in low/task_worker.pyi or low/task_worker_impl.pyi is exercised. Ensure the suite resolves the implementation modules without relying on a package-qualified path that is shadowed by the top-level module namespace, so the contracted postconditions (execute transforms the payload and reports completion, fetch_and_execute dispatches then executes, execution failure raises WorkerExecutionException) and the telemetry/reset invariants (processed_count, last_task_id, is_busy) are actually verified.
